  "notes": "Built from acecqa-services-latest.csv, acecqa-providers-latest.csv, provider-profile.csv, cth-ccs-enforcement-actions.csv, nsw-enforcement-actions.csv, qld-enforcement-actions.csv, sa-enforcement-actions.csv, tas-enforcement-actions.csv, vecra-enforcement-actions.csv, wa-enforcement-actions.csv, abn-details.csv, plus spine-unlisted.csv derived from the same inputs in the same run. Window: 24 calendar months ending 2026-10-28 (the ACECQA snapshot date), inclusive of 2024-10-29. Counts are of published enforcement actions of every type; action_type columns stay separate and prosecutions are not breaches. Rows flagged 'duplicate row in source' are kept but not counted. Coverage: NSW from Jan 2025, VIC from Jan 2026, QLD from 2017 (no keys), CTH rolling 12 months; SA, WA, TAS, NT, ACT not yet collected. Absence of an action is not evidence of safety. Names of providers withheld as likely individuals stay null. ACECQA content is not openly licensed: internal use only. Rows whose SE-/PR- key is absent from the ACECQA export of 2026-10-28 are joined to stub entries listed in spine-unlisted.csv (spine_status not_in_current_register); their identity comes from the enforcement register, they hold no current rating, and they are kept out of the live denominators. One row per unlisted approval key: name, address, suburb, state and postcode are values printed on the enforcement rows that carry the key (most recent date_issued wins; other names in stub_name_variants). Withheld names stay null and the street address of a withheld row is never used. first_seen and last_seen are date_issued dates."
